## Real provider acceptance

A fresh real account-authenticated Codex `exec` run passed through the Tekrion
wrapper on 2026-07-29 using the existing ChatGPT login and a disposable
home/workspace:

- Codex selected a temporary `tekrion_recorder_*` provider;
- the requested file was created and byte-verified;
- the wrapped session completed;
- 84 events and zero recorded errors were retained;
- all four provider requests completed;
- active requests returned to zero;
- provider authentication was recorded only as `chatgpt-account`;
- the workspace final snapshot contained the expected one-file change;
- the disposable daemon was stopped cleanly.

The preceding Codex acceptance also verified share `.tkr` export/import,
read-only imported evidence, and persistence across daemon restart.

Claude subscription/OAuth acceptance remains deferred because native login is
not active. API-key-only Claude provider acceptance is now complete.

The first bounded API-key acceptance on 2026-08-03 exposed a release-blocking
defect: three valid gzip-compressed Anthropic Messages SSE responses were
retained byte-faithfully but normalized as compressed bytes, producing three
`parser.error` events. It also showed that the account-scoped Anthropic
organization response header was retained.

The authorized fix now:

- normalizes a bounded decoded copy of gzip Anthropic JSON/SSE while leaving raw
  forwarded and stored bytes unchanged;
- treats corrupt, unsupported, and over-limit encodings as explicit malformed
  evidence;
- versions the updated Anthropic normalizer as `1.1.0`;
- forbids the Anthropic organization header at both durable schema and proxy
  persistence boundaries; and
- adds storage migration 6 to scrub that header from active historical raw
  exchange records.

A fresh bounded API-key-only Claude Code 2.1.205 acceptance repeated after the
fix. The wrapped run created and byte-verified one 38-byte file and exited
successfully. Three complete gzip SSE responses remained valid compressed raw
evidence and all normalized as `anthropic.messages.sse@1.1.0`, producing the
expected assistant, tool, usage, and completion evidence with zero parser,
capture, transport, or upstream errors. The API key was absent from the active
database, every decoded blob, the repository, and all disposable test-home
files. The Anthropic organization header was absent from persisted raw headers.
A share export applied 46 redactions, imported as `imported-readonly`, and
survived daemon startup. All disposable daemons were stopped.

The complete 2026-08-03 source gate passed formatting, lint, TypeScript, 337
unit tests, the production build, and both packaged end-to-end tests. Focused
gzip, privacy, migration, and recorder coverage passed 100 tests.

The release-gate refresh later on 2026-08-03 found newly reviewed advisories in
the locked development graph. The lock now resolves `brace-expansion` 5.0.9 and
`postcss` 8.5.25. A clean install and high-severity audit reported zero
vulnerabilities. Source gates, package smoke, and two consecutive offline demos
passed with the patched lock. The exact-source benchmark measured 8.004 ms p95
time-to-first-byte overhead, 8.045 ms p95 total overhead, 1.878 ms p95 cockpit
initial-document total, and 101,360 gzip bytes across the three cockpit assets.

